                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dc591b66-8fca-4a6d-bebe-36f27074e5fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e4109f1-1565-3d85-bb67-20d3ad0946d7",
                        "source_sense_id": "aeb28556-3217-3869-b748-a7a6ef8039ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "surfer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "surfer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cd11a20-3068-3fc9-91c7-7d7bf726bace",
                                        "entry_id": "2aa0fc62-bea6-374a-a104-781fb4b239bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who rides a surfboard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5fb96d8-3475-44a0-9be9-32a6e539023c",
                                                "sense_id": "3cd11a20-3068-3fc9-91c7-7d7bf726bace",
                                                "text": "When the surfer has passed the point where the waves are breaking, and is among the waves which are known as “greenbacks”, he may either dive through them or float over them, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26e0bf8f-326d-42d4-a8be-d871217cb1af",
                                                "sense_id": "3cd11a20-3068-3fc9-91c7-7d7bf726bace",
                                                "text": "A road that runs due west from Dale passes the village church and Dale Castle, and a footpath continues to Westdale Bay, a sandy beach used by surfers when the westerlies send great rollers crashing in from the Atlantic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3815197-a3f0-39e9-baef-f9a2b1d65860",
                                        "entry_id": "2aa0fc62-bea6-374a-a104-781fb4b239bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who surfs the Internet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3086f38-ab82-3071-9e0d-cc43ec3f1c3e",
                                        "entry_id": "2aa0fc62-bea6-374a-a104-781fb4b239bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A duck, the surf scoter (Melanitta perspicillata)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e7a7320-c286-43ea-b0e5-72e236284a35",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e4109f1-1565-3d85-bb67-20d3ad0946d7",
                        "source_sense_id": "aeb28556-3217-3869-b748-a7a6ef8039ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "surfeur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "surfeur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c847716-7215-3dd5-97a2-006d2f637a0e",
                                        "entry_id": "2414c906-ac07-3541-9fca-2240cca667a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui surfe, qui pratique le surf."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Snowboard",
                                            "Surf"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96f3fb46-eac0-499d-8fdf-02b387e2e22d",
                                                "sense_id": "6c847716-7215-3dd5-97a2-006d2f637a0e",
                                                "text": "« C’était cool de savoir qu’on accueillait les JO, mais on s’est dit : “Pourvu qu’ils ne nous détruisent pas.” », concède Michaël Vautor, patron d’une entreprise qui amène touristes et surfeurs sur LA vague."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6a5073e-f381-47e7-ae0b-0f69cc05d9ab",
                                                "sense_id": "6c847716-7215-3dd5-97a2-006d2f637a0e",
                                                "text": "Ce modèle corporel informe les cultures balnéaires de la Californie du sud à partir de la fin des années 1900, notamment le long du littoral de Los Angeles (Malibu, Santa Monica…), grâce à des démonstrations de surfeurs hawaïens recrutés par des hommes d’affaires soucieux d’y promouvoir le tourisme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "388fb138-07d0-42c5-92b5-34d1df23853e",
                                                "sense_id": "6c847716-7215-3dd5-97a2-006d2f637a0e",
                                                "text": "Tous les sujets d’actualités y passèrent les uns après les autres : la nouvelle route du littoral, ainsi que les autres projets ruineux de la Région ou du Département ; la pseudo crise du tourisme due aux requins mangeurs de surfeurs…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb17e410-b0ff-38dc-bdbf-dc798228e071",
                                        "entry_id": "2414c906-ac07-3541-9fca-2240cca667a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui surfe sur la toile, qui navigue sur Internet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
